# 📦 Helm

## Overview

Helm is a package manager for Kubernetes that helps manage applications using charts.

---

## Helm Folder Structure

```
mychart/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
├── values-dev.yaml
├── values-prod.yaml
├── charts/
├── templates/
│   ├── deployment.yaml
│   ├── service.yaml
│   ├── ingress.yaml
│   ├── hpa.yaml
│   ├── configmap.yaml
│   ├── secret.yaml
│   ├── _helpers.tpl
│   └── NOTES.txt
├── templates/tests/
└── .helmignore
```

---

## Key Files

### Chart.yaml

Defines metadata.

```yaml
apiVersion: v2
name: web-app
version: 0.1.0
```

---

### values.yaml

Default configuration.

```yaml
replicaCount: 2
image:
  repository: myrepo/web-app
  tag: latest
```

---

### Templates

Dynamic Kubernetes manifests.

```yaml
replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}
image: "{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag }}"
```

---

### _helpers.tpl

Reusable template logic.

```yaml
{{ define "app.name" }}web-app{{ end }}
```

---

# Helm Commands – Practical DevOps Reference

## 📌 Overview

This document provides a production-ready reference for commonly used Helm commands. It is structured for direct usage in GitHub documentation without requiring further edits or formatting.

