# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

* Editing Kubernetes resources directly instead of using Helm
* Not using values files for environment separation
* Skipping dry-run before production deployment
* Large and unstructured values.yaml files
* Not tracking chart versions properly

---

# 🧠 Best Practices

* Use separate values files (`values-dev.yaml`, `values-prod.yaml`)
* Always run `helm lint` before deployment
* Use `--dry-run --debug` for safe deployments
* Version your charts properly
* Keep templates reusable and clean
* Use dependencies instead of reinventing services

---

# 🧠 Summary

* Helm simplifies Kubernetes deployments using charts
* Supports versioning, rollback, and templating
* Essential for managing production-grade applications
* Integrates well with CI/CD pipelines

